The typed config saves the architecture worktree as source root; sibling `pit-v5-controller-runtime-20260907-04` workspace/output/control/response roots; `pit-v5-controller-runtime-20260907/data`; `C:\Program Files\Git\bin\git.exe`; Docker Desktop's `resources\bin\docker.exe`; and `policy_only`. `campaign-launch-input.json` (SHA `db0f6940e85c023c13a7ee2eac3ae2e03ddb50853cd31ed120c1fd7496fde448`) and `operator-paths.json` (SHA `91ee4f145f16d9ca4428d94408c0821eea8e8a676a4ec2b176a5dff148bc6c49`) repeat command/path metadata but are hash-only evidence, not typed authority.

## Per-round config authority

`CampaignRoundLaunchV5` explicitly stores `round_index`, `adapter_config_ref`, owner-token digest, and optional start time (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/operations.py:77-90`). Round 1 reuses the launch config; later rounds derive and create a new typed config before appending the `campaign-round` state (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/operations.py:494-521`). The started state must equal that entry except for its positive start time (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/operations.py:528-566`).

Both `campaign-round` and `campaign-round-started` loaded as `CampaignRoundLaunchV5` with `repair=False`. In each round, replacing only `started_epoch_ms` with `None` makes the started record exactly equal to the round entry; their config references and owner-token digests are equal.

| Round | Canonical round key | Started-state authority SHA-256 | Started-state value SHA-256 | Config reference and SHA-256 | Config executor SHA-256 | Derived owner SHA-256 |
